From 2565fb9d8626800fdbe54c06091c286defc27a6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: eileenthg <40307498+eileenthg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 05:09:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add AI character settings for every built-in maid model

Add 174 settings YAMLs under the built-in model pack, covering all 193 model IDs
across the touhou_little_maid, touhou_little_maid_old and touhou_little_maid_seihou
domains. SettingReader picks these up the same way it picks up
geckolib/settings/winefox.yml.

Alternate skins and cross-pack duplicates of the same character share a single
file through the model_id list, so PC-98 Reimu resolves to the same prompt as the
Windows-era and legacy Bedrock models, PC-98 Yuuka folds into yuuka_kazami.yml,
and Seihou's Mei and Mai share one file.

Each prompt follows the structure winefox.yml established (identity, ability,
home, personality, speech style, likes, relationships and conversation notes) and
is written in English, since PapiReplacer already notes that settings are authored
in English and the model handles output language. Comment lines are stripped by
CharacterSetting#processText, so every content line reads standalone once they are
gone.

Character details are sourced from en.touhouwiki.net infoboxes and Personality
sections. moesumika has no wiki page and is an original prompt for the server
mascot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
